# Everything the loop is forbidden to merge on its own also needs a human
# review on the pull request. These are the same paths as
# `harness.toml [autonomy] blocked_paths` — kept in step with it deliberately.
#
# CODEOWNERS assigns the review. The lane classifier is what actually stops the
# merge. Neither replaces the other: one is a request, one is a gate.

# The loop must not rewrite the loop.
/.github/                 @junglecrunch1212

# The control surface and its enforcement.
/harness.toml             @junglecrunch1212
/scripts/                 @junglecrunch1212

# The only gate the pipeline has lives in the `ci` script, and a new
# dependency is a supply-chain decision.
/package.json             @junglecrunch1212
/package-lock.json        @junglecrunch1212

# A shipped migration has already run against rows that mean something.
/db/migrations/           @junglecrunch1212

# Reserved. If authorization is ever added, it is born blocked.
/kernel/auth/             @junglecrunch1212

# The source of truth and the invariants it declares.
/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md     @junglecrunch1212
/docs/SCHEMA.sql          @junglecrunch1212
/tests/invariants/        @junglecrunch1212
